Braintrust discovered the breach of one of its AWS accounts on 2026-05-04 and disclosed it on 2026-05-05; no source gives the date the attackers got in. The stored keys were org-level AI provider keys, the rotation was a request to every customer rather than a mandate, and the companies named as likely key holders are a Nudge Security executive's estimate, not adjacent SaaS credentials at risk. At least one customer was affected and three others reported suspicious AI provider usage spikes.
